{"id":57226208215724,"type":"album","name":"Fun House","artist":"The Stooges","year":1970,"weight":93,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711107.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-68ee7490-8776-4200-9ef1-d6553eb8ba16/mbid-68ee7490-8776-4200-9ef1-d6553eb8ba16-14524268492.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":7,"country":"US","aoty":97,"aoty_user":83,"yt":"o4GTkpSzRDQ","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-stooges/fun-house","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/6035-the-stooges-funhouse.php"},"desc":"Fun House is the second studio album by American rock band the Stooges. It was released on July 7, 1970, by Elektra Records. Though initially commercially unsuccessful, Fun House developed a strong cult following. Like its predecessor (1969's The Stooges) and its successor (1973's Raw Power), it is generally considered integral in the development of punk rock. In 1969, Elektra Records had released the Stooges' debut album to mixed reviews and mediocre commercial success (peaking at number 106 on the Billboard charts). Company head Jac Holzman believed that MC5, another Michigan-based band, had more potential of success than the Stooges. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":280372946476675,"name":"The Stooges","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Iggy_and_The_Stooges_-_4572393187.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":129644386263637,"type":"genre","name":"Punk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1272,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":109063683126539,"type":"genre","name":"Hard Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":562,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":207419651019004,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":556,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":186201380116213,"type":"genre","name":"classic rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":268,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":51